  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "$z$ is proportional to the square of $x$ and proportional to the square root of $y$. If $z=72$ when $x=2$ and $y=4$, find $z$ when $x=3$ and $y=9$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$z=243$.\n\nUse the joint-proportion model $z=kx^2\\sqrt{y}$.",
      "worked": "Write $z=kx^2\\sqrt{y}$ for some constant $k$. Using $z=72$, $x=2$ and $y=4$,\n$$\\begin{align*}72&=k\\times2^2\\times\\sqrt{4}\\\\72&=8k\\\\k&=9.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $z=9x^2\\sqrt{y}$. When $x=3$ and $y=9$,\n$$\\begin{align*}z&=9\\times3^2\\times\\sqrt{9}\\\\z&=9\\times9\\times3\\\\z&=243.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
